    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p3-q3a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "Complete the table above. List all possible outcomes as ordered pairs $(x,y)$, with the row number first and the column number second.",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$$\\begin{array}{c|cccccc}&1&2&3&4&5&6\\\\\\hline 1&(1,1)&(1,2)&(1,3)&(1,4)&(1,5)&(1,6)\\\\2&(2,1)&(2,2)&(2,3)&(2,4)&(2,5)&(2,6)\\\\3&(3,1)&(3,2)&(3,3)&(3,4)&(3,5)&(3,6)\\\\4&(4,1)&(4,2)&(4,3)&(4,4)&(4,5)&(4,6)\\\\5&(5,1)&(5,2)&(5,3)&(5,4)&(5,5)&(5,6)\\\\6&(6,1)&(6,2)&(6,3)&(6,4)&(6,5)&(6,6)\\end{array}$$",
          "worked": "In each row, hold the first coordinate fixed and let the second coordinate run from $1$ to $6$. This gives $6\\times6=36$ equally likely outcomes.\n\n$$\\begin{array}{c|cccccc}&1&2&3&4&5&6\\\\\\hline 1&(1,1)&(1,2)&(1,3)&(1,4)&(1,5)&(1,6)\\\\2&(2,1)&(2,2)&(2,3)&(2,4)&(2,5)&(2,6)\\\\3&(3,1)&(3,2)&(3,3)&(3,4)&(3,5)&(3,6)\\\\4&(4,1)&(4,2)&(4,3)&(4,4)&(4,5)&(4,6)\\\\5&(5,1)&(5,2)&(5,3)&(5,4)&(5,5)&(5,6)\\\\6&(6,1)&(6,2)&(6,3)&(6,4)&(6,5)&(6,6)\\end{array}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 0
      },
      {
        "id": "p3-q3b",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "Hence, find the probability of the following events.",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p3-q3bi",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "i",
            "prompt": "Only one of the dice shows a 2.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{5}{18}$",
              "worked": "Row $2$ and column $2$ each contribute five outcomes when $(2,2)$ is left out. $$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{exactly one }2)&=\\frac{5+5}{36}\\\\P(\\text{exactly one }2)&=\\frac{5}{18}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3bii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "ii",
            "prompt": "At least one of the dice shows a 2.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{11}{36}$",
              "worked": "Count row $2$ and column $2$, counting their common cell $(2,2)$ once. $$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{at least one }2)&=\\frac{6+6-1}{36}\\\\P(\\text{at least one }2)&=\\frac{11}{36}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3biii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iii",
            "prompt": "Both dice show a 2.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{1}{36}$",
              "worked": "Only the cell $(2,2)$ qualifies. $$P(\\text{both show }2)=\\frac{1}{36}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 11
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3biv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "iv",
            "prompt": "The sum is equal to 7.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{1}{6}$",
              "worked": "The cells $(1,6)$, $(2,5)$, $(3,4)$, $(4,3)$, $(5,2)$ and $(6,1)$ have sum $7$. $$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{sum }7)&=\\frac{6}{36}\\\\P(\\text{sum }7)&=\\frac{1}{6}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 17
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3bv",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "v",
            "prompt": "The sum exceeds 8.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{5}{18}$",
              "worked": "The table has four cells with sum $9$, three with sum $10$, two with sum $11$ and one with sum $12$. $$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{sum}>8)&=\\frac{4+3+2+1}{36}\\\\P(\\text{sum}>8)&=\\frac{5}{18}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 18
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3bvi",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "vi",
            "prompt": "Not rolling double 6.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{35}{36}$",
              "worked": "Double $6$ occurs in just one cell, $(6,6)$. Use its complement. $$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{no double }6)&=1-\\frac{1}{36}\\\\P(\\text{no double }6)&=\\frac{35}{36}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 15
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3bvii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "vii",
            "prompt": "Not rolling a double.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$\\frac{5}{6}$",
              "worked": "The six cells with matching row and column numbers are doubles. Use their complement. $$\\begin{align*}P(\\text{no double})&=1-\\frac{6}{36}\\\\P(\\text{no double})&=\\frac{5}{6}\\end{align*}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 16
          },
          {
            "id": "p3-q3bviii",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "viii",
            "prompt": "The product of the numbers is even.",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": {
                "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
                "version": 1,
                "blocks": [
                  {
